# Rules

## Core Principles

1. Use functional programming paradigm
2. Prefer functions over classes
3. Write testable code
4. Always design types before implementation

## TypeScript Rules

1. Do not use `any`
2. Avoid `unknown`
3. Explicitly type all function inputs and outputs
4. Prefer narrow and precise types
5. Name constants, variables, and functions in `camelCase`
6. Explicitly handle `null`/`undefined`
7. Use `const` over `let`

## React Rules

1. Use only functional components
2. Extract logic into custom hooks
3. Prefer composition over inheritance
4. Separate logic from view, prefer to create more dumb components
5. Do not export anything from component files except the component itself

## Code Organization

1. Keep types separate from implementation
2. Avoid impure functions; use pure functions when possible
3. Do not mutate arguments
4. Always return new values
5. Never mutate data
6. Keep functions small and focused (one responsibility per function)
7. Limit functions to 3–5 logical lines of code (excluding braces, blank lines, and comments)
8. Avoid deep nesting; use early returns
9. Use arrow functions
10. Use descriptive names; do not use single letters or abbreviations
11. One file - one export